# Build context is this "backend" directory for every service's Dockerfile
# (each docker-compose.yml sets `build.context: ..`).

.git
**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/*.md

# Never needed inside an image; deploy config, not app code.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/docker-compose*.yaml
**/Dockerfile

# `infrastructure` here is dual-purpose: a Gradle module (source, copied into every
# image build) AND a home for unrelated standalone ops compose stacks. Only the
# Gradle module is needed to compile — exclude the ops subfolders so they're never
# sent as build context or copied into an image.
infrastructure/monitor/
infrastructure/alloy/
infrastructure/redis/
infrastructure/minio/
infrastructure/postgres/
infrastructure/ldap-local/
